  "narrative": {
    "text": "Figure 2(c): the refined blueprint after the planner model decomposed the stuck nodes further. Rectangles are definitions and ellipses are theorems; dashed arrows mark a statement-level use and solid arrows a proof-level use. Definition nodes taylorKernel, taylorRemainderKernel, taylorPoly, lineMap and lineCurve sit at the top; the target frechet_taylor_integral is the sink at the bottom. New intermediate nodes appear -- taylor_remainder_by_parts, taylor_integral_kernel_base, taylorPoly_succ, ftoc_bochner_on_uIcc and lineCurve_contDiffOn_onSeg -- and every theorem node is light blue, i.e. nothing is yet proved in this version.",
